          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "focus": "Synthesize information from research notes to accomplish a specific rhetorical goal for a given audience",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 4 · Q2",
          "passageTitle": "Rhetorical Synthesis — Q2",
          "passage": "While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Blackberries are fruits that contain ascorbic acid, an essential nutrient for humans.\n• Every 100 grams (g) of blackberries contains 21 milligrams (mg) of ascorbic acid.\n• Many animals can make ascorbic acid in their bodies, but humans cannot.\n• Humans must get ascorbic acid from foods, including fruits and vegetables.\n• Ascorbic acid is also known as vitamin C.",
          "prompt": "The student wants to specify how much vitamin C is in blackberries. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?",
          "options": [
            "Many animals can make ascorbic acid, which is also known as vitamin C, in their bodies, but humans cannot.",
