          "skill": "Rhetorical Synthesis",
          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "focus": "Synthesize information from research notes to accomplish a specific rhetorical goal for a given audience",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 4 · Q3",
          "passageTitle": "Rhetorical Synthesis — Q3",
          "passage": "While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Sister cities are pairs of cities that form social or legal partnerships to promote each other's cultures.\n• Previously known as \"town twinning,\" the concept of sister cities evolved in Europe after WORLD WAR II as a way to repair bonds between cities.\n• Many cities in New York State maintain such partnerships with cities around the world.\n• Rhinebeck, New York, and Larreynaga, Nicaragua, became sister cities in 1989.",
          "prompt": "The student wants to emphasize the duration of Rhinebeck and Larreynaga's sister city relationship. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?",
          "options": [
