          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 4 · Q45",
          "passageTitle": "Rhetorical Synthesis — Q45",
          "passage": "While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• The El Pinito Mountains are a mountain range located in northwestern Mexico.\n• The range is one of the dozens of \"sky islands\" in the southwestern US and northwestern Mexico.\n• A sky island is an isolated mountain range whose environment differs drastically from that of the surrounding lowlands.\n• The US Forest Service (USFS) said, \"The mountains are 'islands' surrounded by deserts that are seas.\"\n• The USFS said, \"Each Sky Island is a unique ecosystem.\"",
          "prompt": "The student wants to explain what a sky island is. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?",
          "options": [
            "The USFS considers the El Pinito Mountains to be a \"unique ecosystem.\"",
