          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 4 · Q48",
          "passageTitle": "Rhetorical Synthesis — Q48",
          "passage": "While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Birds of Northern South America is an identification guidebook by ornithologists Robin Restall, Clemencia Rodner, and Miguel Lentino.\n• It lists the thirty-five hummingbird species found in Suriname.\n• The sooty-capped hermit is a large hummingbird found in Suriname.\n• It is identifiable by its distinctive facial markings and its long, black, curved bill.\n• The fiery-tailed awlbill is a small hummingbird found in Suriname.\n• It is identifiable by its mostly dark green color and its short, black, upturned bill.",
          "prompt": "Which choice most effectively uses information from the given sentences to emphasize a difference between the two birds?",
          "options": [
            "The sooty-capped hermit and the fiery-tailed awlbill are two of the thirty-five hummingbird species found in Suriname.",
